Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: the page sees the claimed adapter, not SwiftShader

When SwiftShader stands in for the claimed adapter, the page reads the
claimed features and limits, and isFallbackAdapter is false as on the
real device. A device requested within the claimed limits works within
what SwiftShader can run, and going past what SwiftShader has fails with
an error, like a WebGL limit the driver refuses. A request beyond the
claimed limits fails with the real device's message, and asking for a
fallback adapter returns none.

